142b6f0c08e645ef9507f6d880be44e518c39043:SKILL.md:3:description: "Deep-research method (調査) — question framing, source hierarchy, citation chaining, claim-vs-source verification. Triggers: 'research this', 'deep research', 'verify this claim', 'primary source', 'citation chain'. Anti-trigger: NOT bounty-program scope (kasegi), NOT model-quality claims (kengaku), NOT external live-target fetching without operator approval. Rank: shonen."
142b6f0c08e645ef9507f6d880be44e518c39043:SKILL.md:17:| Research a question | question framing → source hierarchy → chain → claim check | starting from a search box with no question | a research record with a declared question |
142b6f0c08e645ef9507f6d880be44e518c39043:corpus/knowledge/archived-export-intake.md:89:| CL-07 | inference | general | export-unverified | SKILL.md:17 | | answer to the question, YES in part, the archive alone supports reusable research-method claims about FORM, question framing before search CL-02, hedged negatives as corrective labels CL-03, inline evidence-versus-rule labeling CL-04, kept-unresolved chains CL-06, NO for content, the same archive cannot verify any cited domain claim without external sources, every chain terminates unwalkably, so the export-unverified tier is load-bearing and the exports never enter as primary sources |
142b6f0c08e645ef9507f6d880be44e518c39043:corpus/knowledge/japanese-search-record-r38-amendment-2026-10-23.md:11:- **The protocol-writing paragraph names PRISMA-P, its size and the search's features.** It says PRISMA-P holds 17 items regarded as the minimum elements of a review protocol (`要素と考えられる，17 項目が含まれている`, `S112`, char 10016), and gives among its examples the search's features: "検索の特徴（検索期間" (`S112`, char 10140) and "検索期間，言語制限" (`S112`, char 10146), beside eligibility criteria and whether unpublished material and abstracts are included; the paragraph goes on that these must be specified (`明記することが`, `S112`, char 10200).
142b6f0c08e645ef9507f6d880be44e518c39043:corpus/knowledge/quality-control-guideline-issued-text-r48.md:15:- **1.文献研究的质量控制: what the instrument requires of a search.** The subsection "1.文献研究的质量控制" (`S118`, char 9938) heads the methods chapter (the extraction's pp. 16–17). For guideline-type evidence it sets an evidence floor, "对于循证指南类证据，应获取最新的、权威的且已公开发表" (char 10109); for research evidence it hands the criteria to the evaluation theme with PICOS as an option, "证据，应根据评价主题确定纳入与排除标准，可基于“PICOS”" (char 10167); it requires several databases in both languages and two independent screeners, "数据库应包括多个中、英文专业数据库。由两名研究人员独立筛" (char 10360), a third arbitrating, "选文献，如遇分歧，则由第三方协助判断" (char 10390), and a flow chart with a count and a reason at each step, "确定最终是否纳入。根据文献筛选流程制定流程图，注明每环节" (char 10450).
142b6f0c08e645ef9507f6d880be44e518c39043:corpus/knowledge/quality-control-guideline-issued-text-r48.md:26:- **The inclusion rule belongs to the evaluation theme, with PICOS optional and the evidence floor class-specific.** `S118` reads "证据，应根据评价主题确定纳入与排除标准，可基于“PICOS”" — 可, not 应 — and it tightens the floor for guideline-type evidence only, "对于循证指南类证据，应获取最新的、权威的且已公开发表"。 So a claim that this instrument mandates PICOS, or that it sets one evidence floor for all classes, is not this text's.
